    "sample_answer": "Choosing a career is one of the most important decisions in a person's life. While some people prefer to stay in one job forever, I believe that people should change their careers at least once during their lives. This change helps individuals find true happiness and develop new skills for a better future. \nFirst of all, changing careers allows people to escape from stress and find a job that makes them truly happy. In life, many people choose a job just because they need money, but after many years, they feel completely exhausted and bored. Instead of staying in an unhappy place, changing to a new career recharges their energy and brings joy back to their daily life. For example, in the past, I worked as a stressed office staff for a small company. I hated sitting in front of a computer all day, so I decided to change my career and became a sales clerk at a clothing brand called The ABC. This choice made me feel really happy because I could talk to friendly customers every day. Therefore, a career change is necessary for personal happiness.\nSecondly, changing careers helps people challenge themselves and learn useful new skills. Staying in one job for too long can make a person lazy and afraid of facing hard problems. In reality, real personal growth always happens when individuals are brave enough to make mistakes, face failures in a new environment, and try to learn again. When people move to a new career, they have to learn how to adapt and solve new tasks. This process destroys their fear of change and builds their confidence to handle any difficulties in life.\nIn conclusion, although staying in one job brings safety, people definitely should change their careers during their lives. The freedom to choose a new path helps us reduce stress and grow much stronger. Therefore, individuals should not be afraid of change if they want to improve their lives and work with passion.",
