    "has_sample": true,
    "sample_answer": "Government investment plays a crucial role in improving the quality of citizens' lives. While spending money on sports for young people has certain health benefits, I firmly believe that the government should prioritize investing in public transportation. This decision brings significant advantages in terms of reducing traffic issues and protecting the environment.\nFirst of all, developing a modern public transportation system effectively reduces traffic congestion and saves money for residents. In major cities, daily traffic jams cause severe delays, making people late for work and school. If the government builds more subway lines and electric bus routes, more people will choose public transit over personal vehicles like cars or motorbikes. For example, in my city, the government recently opened a new metro line. Since then, my daily travel time to the office has decreased by twenty minutes, and I do not have to worry about traffic jams during rush hours anymore.\nSecondly, investing in public transit is the best way to reduce environmental pollution. Personal vehicles emit a massive amount of greenhouse gases every day, which leads to poor air quality and climate change. Public buses and trains can carry hundreds of passengers at the same time, which greatly lowers the total amount of carbon emissions per person. By making public transport cleaner, cheaper, and more convenient, the government can encourage green habits among all citizens, including the younger generation. \nIn conclusion, although supporting sports programs for young people is important for health, I prefer government investment in public transportation. This infrastructure spending provides long-term benefits by solving traffic congestion and creating a cleaner environment for everyone.",
