    "id": "P3_28",
    "category": "workplace",
    "category_vi": "Môi trường công sở",
    "topic": "Working from home vs. Working in an office",
    "difficulty": "medium",
    "exam_date": "Authentic Real Exam",
    "prompt": "Do you agree or disagree with the following statement? “Working from home is better than working in an office.” Use specific reasons and examples to support your opinion.",
    "prompt_vi": "Bạn đồng ý hay không đồng ý với nhận định sau: \"Làm việc tại nhà tốt hơn làm việc tại văn phòng công ty\"? Hãy sử dụng các lý lẽ và ví dụ xác đáng để bảo vệ cho ý kiến của mình.",
    "has_sample": true,
    "sample_answer": "In recent years, the rapid advancement of digital communication technology has dramatically transformed the traditional work environment. While many employees appreciate the structure of corporate offices, I firmly agree that working from home is significantly better than working in a conventional office setting due to greater flexibility, increased productivity, and enhanced work-life balance.\n\nFirst and foremost, remote work saves a substantial amount of time and energy that would otherwise be wasted on daily commuting. In major metropolitan areas, employees often spend hours stuck in heavy traffic or crowded public transit, which causes unnecessary stress and exhaustion before the workday even begins. By working from home, professionals can utilize this saved time to rest, exercise, or prepare nutritious meals, thereby starting their work with high energy and focus. For example, my colleague used to spend two hours commuting each day; since transitioning to remote work, he has reported lower stress levels and higher job satisfaction.\n\nFurthermore, remote working environments often provide fewer workplace interruptions and greater autonomy, leading to higher overall productivity. In a typical office, constant chatter, impromptu meetings, and background noise can easily disrupt deep concentration. In contrast, working in a personalized home office allows individuals to create an optimal workspace tailored to their personal preferences, enabling them to complete complex tasks more efficiently. In addition, the flexibility to manage one's own schedule enables workers to spend quality time with their families, fostering a healthier work-life balance without sacrificing professional performance.\n\nIn conclusion, although office work fosters in-person social interactions, the benefits of working from home in terms of saving commute time, boosting individual focus, and enhancing personal well-being are far superior. Therefore, I believe that telecommuting represents a much more advantageous working model for modern professionals.",
